diff --git a/docs/ops/ops-logging.md b/docs/ops/ops-logging.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..86568bc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/ops-logging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Ops Logging Lanes
+
+The application uses three distinct logging channels to separate concerns and keep observability manageable.
+
+## 1. Archive (`daily`)
+
+*Purpose*: Routine application logs from *debug* through *error*.
+
+*Location*: `storage/logs/laravel.log`.
+
+*Rotation*: Daily, keep 14 days (configurable via `LOG_DAILY_DAYS`).
+
+*Typical Usage*: Log general application activity, errors, and any non‑critical diagnostics.
+
+## 2. Audit (`audit`)
+
+*Purpose*: Durable trail of **who changed what** – e.g. membership role changes, subscription transitions, login lockouts.
+
+*Location*: `storage/logs/audit.log`.
+
+*Rotation*: Daily, keep 90 days (configurable via `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS`).
+
+*Typical Usage*: Record privileged changes and user actions that must be auditable.
+
+## 3. Alert (`DiscordOpsAlert`)
+
+*Purpose*: Human‑pageable ops incidents that require immediate attention.
+
+*Delivery*: Sends a single message to a Discord incoming webhook via the `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert` service.
+
+*When to use*:
+- Job retries exhausted.
+- Critical webhook or external integration fails.
+- Application limits or throttling blocks a feature.
+
+*Never use* for regular application logs or audit events.
+
+---
+
+### Quick Decision Guide
+| Situation | Use Archive | Use Audit | Use Discord Alert |
+|-----------|-------------|-----------|------------------|
+| Routine error | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ |
+| User role change | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ |
+| Payment gateway webhook fails | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ |
+| Application startup crash | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ |
+
+---
+
+### Environment Variables
+```
+LOG_DAILY_DAYS=14
+LOG_AUDIT_DAYS=90
+LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL=info
+DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
+```
